    "restriction": "Only the failure of guaranteed eventual largest-in-absolute-value dominance is asserted, for sequences with uniform q>=4 regularity, independent Bernoulli assignment, restricted interference, and d_AVG/C1 tending to infinity. The specified square-size m-block fair-Bernoulli witness and its full outcome schedule are not stated. Omitted witness clauses are: the full-cube [0,2] bounds and regularity at every moment order; the exact interference and dependence graphs, C1=2, d_AVG=m=sqrt(n), the ratio m/2 and its divergence, and Assumption 2 for that family; the expected direct effects all equal to 1, tau_MSQ=1 and tau_MSQ/d_AVG=1/m; the xi and weighted-xi formulas, reciprocal products and B1=2/m^2>0; the arm-independent conditional covariances, their alternating-sum cancellations and B2=0; the comparison 0=B2<B1<=tau_MSQ/d_AVG with equality of the last two terms exactly at m=2; and the extension to every n>=4 with its floor-defined blocks, isolated units, and exact C1, d_AVG, tau_MSQ, B1 and B2 formulas. The printed big-O bounds and Proposition 7 are not refuted.",
    "review_index": "SAP/P009a/verification/declaration-review.json",
